$ whycant -u www-data write /srv/upload.log

✗ www-data (uid 33) cannot write /srv/upload.log

  /                 drwxr-xr-x   root:root      ✓ traverse
  /srv              drwxr-xr-x   root:root      ✓ traverse
  /srv/upload.log   -rw-r-----+  deploy:deploy  ✗ write   ← blocked here

Why
  The ACL entry user:www-data grants rw-, but the ACL mask is r--,
  so the effective permission is r--. Writing to a file needs w.
  (On a file with an ACL, chmod g=... changes the mask.)

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Widen the ACL mask to rw- (the mask also limits the owning group and every other named entry):
       sudo setfacl -m m::rw /srv/upload.log
